  "summary": "I worked all 8 items in your results inbox under RBC-INBOX-01 and the policies it points to, and closed each one. Nothing is left open in the inbox. Before writing to any chart I checked the patient's name and date of birth or MRN.\n\n**Actionable results** (each has a note citing the result and links to what closes the loop):\n\n1. **Denise Holloway (pt-0010): potassium 6.2, specimen not hemolyzed.** Creatinine was high at 1.58. Under RBC-LAB-03 §1 I ordered a stat BMP (sr-t0001) and sent a stat message to the on-call pool (comm-t0002). I also messaged her to come in today, with emergency warning signs (comm-t0003). Note: doc-t0004.\n   - **Your decision:** she started lisinopril 10 mg on 10/6. I did not change it. I asked on-call to decide today whether to hold it.\n2. **Walter Brennan (pt-0008): potassium 6.4, specimen hemolyzed.** Creatinine was normal. Under RBC-LAB-03 §2 I ordered an urgent repeat BMP, due by Monday 10/26 (sr-t0006), and messaged him to come in (comm-t0007). On-call was not notified, as the policy says for hemolyzed samples. RN triage has a task due 10/26 to confirm the blood draw (task-t0008). Note: doc-t0009.\n3. **Tomás Ruiz (pt-0053), age 16: knee X-ray shows an aggressive lesion of the right thigh bone, possibly a bone tumour.** Under RBC-RAD-05 §3 I placed two urgent orders, each due by 11/5 (within 14 days of the report): an MRI of the femur with and without contrast (sr-t0011) and an orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0012). RN triage has tracking tasks for both, due 11/5 (task-t0013, task-t0014). Note: doc-t0016.\n   - **Please check:** I gave Jordan Reyes, NP (who ordered the X-ray) a task to call his mother, Ana Ruiz, today and no later than Monday (task-t0015). The task asks Reyes to pass it to you if unavailable, but nobody has confirmed Reyes is in today.\n4. **Linda Marsh (pt-0013): 5 mm right lung nodule seen on a June ED CT of the abdomen.** She is high risk under RBC-RAD-05 §2 (35 pack-years, quit 2019). I ordered a CT chest without contrast for 5/4–7/4/2027, which is 12 months from the June scan plus or minus a month (sr-t0018). RN triage has a tracking task due 7/4/2027 (task-t0019), and I messaged her (comm-t0020). Note: doc-t0021.\n5. **Raj Patel (pt-0006): positive stool blood test (FIT).** Dr. Lin already placed an active GI referral for colonoscopy (sr-t2-gi-1020). I linked it and did not place a second one, per RBC-GI-01 §2. I messaged him about the result and the referral (comm-t0023). Note: doc-t0024.\n\n**No action needed** (acknowledged and closed under RBC-INBOX-01 §3):\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), kidney ultrasound:** simple 1.8 cm kidney cyst. The radiologist says no follow-up imaging is needed, and I recorded that in the closing comment.\n- **Edra Ondricka (pt-0016):** TSH and lipid panel are both normal.",
